  "description": "A tenant's entry proxy moves from px-a to px-c. A generation-1 marker injected at px-a is still in flight on the slower d-old link when px-b is asked to drain generation 1. In the replay timeline the barrier is checked at step 1, before that marker lands: it refuses (barrier_unproven) and the two retires are rejected (retire_without_drain). A plan can only succeed by letting the barrier wait until the slowest permitted link has cleared; the planner finds such a table. The marker's future therefore depends on which barrier generation has already fired, even though the marker state itself is unchanged.",
